resolve::misplaced-attribute

  × `#[linear]` applies only to structs, other than bit-field structs
   ╭─[linear_attribute_misplaced.ers:5:1]
 4 │ // value (ADR 0101).
 5 │ #[linear]
   · ────┬────
   ·     ╰── not allowed on a bit-field struct
 6 │ struct Flags: u8 { ready: bool at 0 }
   ╰────
  help: `#[linear]` makes the values of a struct linear: each must be consumed before the function
        holding it returns, and none is overwritten; no other item has values (ADR 0101)
resolve::misplaced-attribute

  × `#[linear]` applies only to structs, other than bit-field structs
   ╭─[linear_attribute_misplaced.ers:8:1]
 7 │ 
 8 │ #[linear]
   · ────┬────
   ·     ╰── not allowed on an enum
 9 │ enum Color: u8 { Red = 0, Green = 1 }
   ╰────
  help: `#[linear]` would bind nobody on an enum: its variants are as visible as the enum, so any
        module that sees it could build a value and take it apart with `match`; an enum is linear
        by holding a linear value (ADR 0101)
